===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sek-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|sector}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|sĕk'tər}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛk.təɹ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sector.wav|Audio (UK)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛktə(ɹ)}}

===Noun===
[[Image:Circle slices.svg|thumb|right|A geometric sector, to the left.]]
{{en-noun}}

# [[section]]
# [[zone]] (designated area).
# {{lb|en|geometry}} part of a [[circle]], extending to the [[center]]
# {{lb|en|computer hardware}} fixed-sized unit (traditionally 512 bytes) of sequential data stored on a [[track]] of a digital medium (compare to [[block]])
# {{lb|en|military}} an area [[designated]] by [[boundaries]] within which a [[unit]] operates, and for which it is [[responsible]]
# {{lb|en|military}} one of the [[subdivisions]] of a [[coastal]] [[frontier]]
# {{lb|en|science fiction}} a [[fictional]] [[region]] of [[space]] designated for [[navigational]] or [[governance]] purposes.
# {{lb|en|calculation}} an instrument consisting of two rulers of equal length joined by a hinge.
# a field of economic activity
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-28|author={{w|Joris Luyendijk}}
|volume=189|issue=3|page=21|magazine={{w|The Guardian Weekly}}
|title=[http://www.guardian.co.uk/commentisfree/joris-luyendijk-banking-blog/2013/jun/19/banking-britain-beyond-control Our banks are out of control]
|passage=Seeing the British establishment struggle with the financial '''sector''' is like watching an alcoholic who still resists the idea that something drastic needs to happen for him to turn his life around. Until 2008 there was denial over what finance had become. When a series of bank failures made this impossible, there was widespread anger, leading to the public humiliation of symbolic figures.}}
#: {{ux|en|public '''sector''';&nbsp; private '''sector'''}}
# {{lb|en|engineering}} A [[toothed]] [[gear]] whose [[face]] is the [[arc]] of a [[circle]].
# {{lb|en|motor racing}} A [[fixed]], [[continuous]] section of the [[track]], such that sectors do not overlap but all sectors make up the whole track.
# {{lb|en|climbing}} An [[area]] to go rock climbing, often consisting of various [[crag]]s

